<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Retrieval quality of various methods on <span id="S4.T3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Flickr2.4M</span>. CoCa and Blip2 are used to generate textual descriptions; <span id="S4.T3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000080;">L</span> (Low), <span id="S4.T3.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;">M</span> (Medium), and <span id="S4.T3.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#800000;">H</span> (High) indicate the quality conditions; and Ctrl specifies whether the method enables controllable retrieval over quality. For both average relevance (Ave Rel) and average aesthetics (Ave Aes), higher values indicate better retrieval quality.</figcaption>
